1. Models trained by this project (src/trubeat/models/)
-------------------------------------------------------

faceswap.joblib
  The face-swap detector v2 (round 4, docs/13 §10), shown as evidence
  only: a logistic regression over frozen CLIP ViT-B/16 features (CLS
  token and patch mean) of face crops. It was trained on:
    - FaceForensics++ c23 and c40 train + val (original, Deepfakes,
      Face2Face, FaceShifter, FaceSwap, NeuralTextures), each also
      re-encoded four ways (docs/13 §3.2);
    - DF40 fakes of eight face-swap methods on FaceForensics++ train/val
      identities (BlendFace, E4S, FaceDancer, FaceSwap, FSGAN, InSwapper,
      MobileSwap, SimSwap).
  DeepFakeDetection, Celeb-DF v2, UADFV and the DF40 test sets were test
  sets only. It uses no OpenVid-1M clips (docs/13 §6.6 item 9). It
  replaced the round-3 detector (docs/12 §9) on 2026-11-08.
  Terms: FaceForensics++ (section 4): non-commercial research and
  educational use only. DF40 (section 4): CC BY-NC 4.0; attribution:
  Z. Yan et al., "DF40: Toward Next-Generation Deepfake Detection",
  NeurIPS 2024 Datasets and Benchmarks Track.

detector.joblib
  The pulse-consistency face-swap check (G2, reports/g2_detector.md): a
  logistic regression over rPPG consistency features, trained and tuned on
  the FaceForensics++ c23 train and validation splits.
  Terms: FaceForensics++: non-commercial research and educational use only.

aigen.joblib
  The AI-video detector (docs/11 §9): a logistic regression over frozen
  DINOv2 ViT-S/14 features. Training data, as recorded in the bundle:
  AIGVDBench (3,721 clips), Rapidata text-to-video sets (1,492 clips) and
  157 FaceForensics++ c23 original (real) train/val clips.
  Terms: FaceForensics++ clips are part of its training data, so it is for
  non-commercial research and educational use only. AIGVDBench is
  CC BY 4.0 and the Rapidata sets are Apache-2.0 (section 4).

Other files in src/trubeat/models/ written by this project, such as
claims.json (the measured numbers the app may quote), are covered by the
MIT License with the code.


