(pyproject.toml names these terms LicenseRef-FaceForensics-NonCommercial)
  Terms of use: https://kaldir.vc.in.tum.de/faceforensics_tos.pdf
  Among them:
    1. "Researcher shall use the Database only for non-commercial research
       and educational purposes."
    4. "Researcher may provide research associates and colleagues with
       access to the Database provided that they first agree to be bound
       by these terms and conditions."
    6. "If Researcher is employed by a for-profit, commercial entity,
       Researcher's employer shall also be bound by these terms and
       conditions, ..."
  The terms do not mention trained models; this project applies them to
  every model trained with the data (section 1). The data itself is never
  redistributed here.
  A. Rössler, D. Cozzolino, L. Verdoliva, C. Riess, J. Thies and
  M. Nießner, "FaceForensics++: Learning to Detect Manipulated Facial
  Images", ICCV 2019.
  N. Dufour, A. Gully et al., "DeepFakes Detection Dataset by Google &
  JigSaw", 2019.

DF40 (training fakes of the face-swap detector v2, faceswap.joblib)
  Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International, for the
  dataset and its code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
  Z. Yan, T. Yao, S. Chen, Y. Zhao, X. Fu, J. Zhu, D. Luo, L. Yuan,
  C. Wang, S. Ding et al., "DF40: Toward Next-Generation Deepfake
